### SSML for Dragon HD Omni style control with Express-As

Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/speech-service/high-definition-voices

This SSML example showcases the 'mstts:express-as' element in Dragon HD Omni to control voice style using natural language descriptions. It allows for nuanced emotional expression by specifying a style like 'sick'.

```ssml
<speak version="1.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts" xml:lang="en-US">
  <voice name="en-us-ava:DragonHDOmniLatestNeural">
    <mstts:express-as style="sick">
      Ugh… I'm not feeling so great today. My head's pounding, and even my voice sounds like it's been through a blender. I think I need to lie down for a bit… maybe some soup would help.
    </mstts:express-as>
  </voice>
</speak>
```

