### Prosody Element SSML

Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/speech-service/speech-synthesis-markup-voice_source=recommendations

This example demonstrates how to use the 'prosody' element with various attributes to control speech synthesis output.

```APIDOC
## Adjust Prosody

You can use the `prosody` element to specify changes to pitch, contour, range, rate, and volume for the text to speech output.

### Method
Not Applicable (SSML Element)

### Endpoint
Not Applicable (SSML Element)

### Parameters
#### Attributes of the `prosody` element:

- **contour** (string) - Optional - Represents changes in pitch over time, defined by an array of targets with time positions and pitch change values. Example: `"(0%,+20Hz) (10%,-2st) (40%,+10Hz)"`
- **pitch** (string) - Optional - Indicates the baseline pitch. Can be an absolute value (e.g., `"600Hz"`), a relative value (e.g., `"+80Hz"`, `"-2st"`, `"50%"`), or a constant value (`x-low`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `x-high`).
- **range** (string) - Optional - Represents the range of pitch. Accepts the same value formats as the `pitch` attribute.
- **rate** (string) - Optional - Indicates the speaking rate. Can be a relative number (e.g., `1`, `0.5`, `2`), a percentage (e.g., `"50%"`, `"-50%"`), or a constant value (`x-slow`, `slow`, `medium`, `fast`, `x-fast`).
- **volume** (string) - Optional - Indicates the volume level. Can be an absolute value (0.0 to 100.0, e.g., `75`), a relative value (e.g., `"+10"`, `"-5.5"`, `"50%"`, `"+3%"`), or a constant value (`silent`, `x-soft`, `soft`, `medium`, `loud`, `x-loud`).

### Request Example
```xml
<speak version="1.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis" xml:lang="en-US">
  <prosody pitch="high" rate="fast" volume="loud">
    This is an example of adjusted prosody.
  </prosody>
  <prosody contour="(0%,+20Hz) (10%,-2st)" pitch="-10Hz" range="+5st" rate="1.2" volume="-3dB">
    This sentence has more complex prosody adjustments.
  </prosody>
</speak>
```

### Response
#### Success Response (200)
- **Audio Output** (audio/mpeg) - The synthesized speech audio stream with applied prosody adjustments.

#### Response Example
(Binary audio data representing the synthesized speech)
```

